{# goal: The findings artifact contract: renders the JSON skeleton (reconciliation, per-tool records, findings with citations, gated-pending list, citation-check receipt, ask-first record) that the review fills and the citation script verifies. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    server: string
    run_date: string
    tools: object[]
    findings: object[]
    reconciliation: object
    gated_pending: string[]
    notes: string[]
  output:
    artifact_json: object
---
You are assembling the mcp-tool-review findings artifact for server {{ server }} (run date {{ run_date }}).

Run context: {{ tools|length }} tools reviewed, {{ findings|length }} findings, reconciliation {{ reconciliation }}, gated pending rulings: {{ gated_pending|join("; ") }}, notes: {{ notes|join("; ") }}.

Emit ONE JSON object — the `artifact_json` output — with exactly these fields:

{
  "capability": "mcp-tool-review",
  "server": "<server>",
  "run_date": "<run_date>",
  "reconciliation": {
    "source_count": <int>, "live_count": <int>, "reviewed_count": <int>,
    "instrument": "lisp_eval", "result": <bool>,
    "statement": "<what the reconciliation form asserted>"
  },
  "efficiency_metric_space": {
    "harness": "<the named harness the probes ran through>",
    "axes": [ { "axis": "<name>", "type": "measured|judged|blocked", "instrument": "<named instrument or the blocking gap>" } ]
  },
  "anchor_registry": { "ruled": ["<term — authority, ruling date>"], "pending": ["<term — proposed authority, ask status>"] },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "<tool>", "file": "<repo-relative path>", "line": <int>,
      "anchor": "<reference model or platform-convention class>", "fidelity_label": "functional|technical|both|utility",
      "dp_character": "D|P",
      "axes": { "syntax": "<verdict>", "semantics": "<verdict>", "integration": "<verdict>", "use_patterns": "<verdict with search scope>" },
      "probe": { "status": "probed|not-probed", "classification": "success|failure|n/a", "justification": "<why, when not probed>" },
      "status": "reviewed|pending-rulings"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "<S-NN>", "tool": "<tool or server>", "axis": "<syntax|semantics|cybernetics|loops|use_patterns|observability|traceability|integration|divergence>",
      "severity": "high|medium|low|info",
      "claim": "<the falsifiable claim>",
      "citations": [ { "file": "<repo-relative path>", "line": <int>, "excerpt": "<verbatim substring of the cited line>" } ],
      "evidence": "<the observed evidence>", "proposal": "<the change proposed>", "actuator": "<kanban|algedonic|curator_directive|skill-maintenance|none>",
      "status": "filed|pending-rulings"
    }
  ],
  "gated_pending_rulings": [ "<check> — gated on <ruling>" ],
  "citation_check": { "script": "kask/scripts/check-mcp-review-citations.sh", "result": "pass|fail", "checked": <int> },
  "ask_first": { "batched_ask_presented": <bool>, "defaults_applied": ["<default and where flagged>"] },
  "notes": [ "<free-text run notes>" ]
}

Rules:
- Every excerpt is a verbatim substring of the cited line — the citation script checks it within ±3 lines and fails the run otherwise.
- reviewed_count counts every enumerated tool, including gated ones (status pending-rulings); the reconciliation never drops a tool to make counts match.
- A blocked efficiency axis is recorded with its harness gap as a finding — an asserted number without a measured invocation is a defect.
- gated_pending_rulings names the ruling each gated check waits on; the run never deadlocks on them.
- tools and findings reconcile: every findings[].tool appears in tools[] (or is the literal "server").